---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro'
import FinalCTA from '../components/blocks/CTA/FinalCTA.astro'

const SEO = {
	title: 'How to Update Your WordPress Site with AI | Frontman',
	description:
		'Install Frontman, connect your AI provider, and describe a change to your existing WordPress site. Inspect the result beside chat and understand when edits go live.'
}
---

<Layout title={SEO.title} description={SEO.description}>
	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 pb-16 pt-24 text-white md:pt-32">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl">From “this needs changing”<br />to a changed WordPress page.</h1>
			<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">You bring the marketing direction. Frontman handles the WordPress edits. Work from the page instead of translating every request into an agency brief or page-builder instructions.</p>
			<Button size="lg" style="primary" link="https://wordpress.org/plugins/frontman-agentic-ai-editor/" classes="mt-8">Get Frontman for WordPress</Button>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-white px-6 py-16 text-neutral-950 md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Connect your existing site.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">You need WordPress 6.0+, PHP 7.4+, and administrator access. If you cannot install plugins, ask your site administrator to handle installation.</p>
			<ol class="mt-8 list-decimal space-y-6 pl-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">
				<li><strong class="text-neutral-950">Install and activate the plugin.</strong> In WordPress, open Plugins → Add New Plugin. Search for Frontman Agentic AI Editor.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-neutral-950">Open Frontman and sign in.</strong> Use the Frontman entry in the WordPress admin menu. Sign in with GitHub or Google.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-neutral-950">Connect your AI provider.</strong> Arrange Frontman service access and connect a supported provider account or key. Provider access and costs are separate.</li>
			</ol>
			<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 font-semibold text-violet-800">
				<a href="/docs/integrations/wordpress/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">WordPress setup guide</a>
				<a href="/docs/api-keys/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">AI-provider setup</a>
				<a href="/pricing/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">Pricing and trial details</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 py-16 text-white md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Start with one update.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Try a headline or one Elementor section on a staging copy first. You do not need to begin with a redesign.</p>
			<ol class="mt-8 list-decimal space-y-8 pl-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">
				<li><strong class="text-white">Describe the outcome.</strong> Open the page in Frontman's preview. Select an element when useful, then explain the change in chat.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-white">Inspect the changed page.</strong> Frontman uses WordPress-native tools to make the edits. Check the copy, layout, and links in context.</li>
				<li><strong class="text-white">Refine and check mobile.</strong> Ask for a focused adjustment. Review the page at the screen sizes your visitors use.</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="mt-8 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-300">You decide the message and judge the result. Some requests need more than one pass.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-white px-6 py-16 text-neutral-950 md:py-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Know when an edit goes live.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">Writes affect the WordPress installation you connect. On a live site, published content can change immediately—before you finish reviewing it. Preview is not a universal approval gate.</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">Start with staging and a backup. Draft publication and staging promotion still use your normal WordPress process. Frontman does not provide a separate approval step for every edit.</p>
			<p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-600">Recovery depends on the change. Elementor snapshots and applicable WordPress revisions cover some changes, but there is no universal undo.</p>
			<a href="/docs/integrations/wordpress/#confirmation-and-rollback" class="copy-link mt-6 inline-block font-semibold text-violet-800 underline underline-offset-4">Read confirmation and recovery details</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="bg-neutral-950 px-6 py-16 text-white">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
			<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">See how a marketing lead used it.</h2>
			<p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-300">Guy Leshno reported redesigning AutonomyAI's existing Elementor site despite having no prior WordPress experience. He kept ownership of positioning, content, stakeholder feedback, and final review.</p>
			<a href="/blog/autonomyai-wordpress-redesign-case-study/" class="copy-link mt-6 inline-block font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Read the AutonomyAI customer story</a>
			<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-neutral-300">One customer-reported project, documented by Frontman—not a guaranteed result.</p>
			<p class="mt-8 border-t border-white/15 pt-6 text-base leading-7 text-neutral-300">Using Next.js, Astro, or Vite instead? <a href="/frameworks/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">Follow the framework workflow</a>. Developers install the integration, review source changes, run tests, and deploy. <a href="/docs/reference/architecture/" class="copy-link underline underline-offset-4">Technical architecture</a> is documented separately.</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<FinalCTA
		link="https://wordpress.org/plugins/frontman-agentic-ai-editor/"
		title="Keep WordPress. Take ownership of the next change."
		description="Install the plugin on a staging copy, connect your AI provider, and start with one update. See pricing for service access and separate provider costs."
		buttonLabel="Get Frontman for WordPress"
	/>
</Layout>

<style>
	section h2 { color: inherit; }
</style>
